{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an image-only model using resnet50 encoder without RNA data or fusion, achieving validation accuracy of 0.2079 and F1 of 0.1718. The results suggest image data alone performs significantly worse than RNA-based baselines (e.g., 0.6530 accuracy for scvi_n200), indicating limited utility of image data in this setting. The exact contribution of the image encoder versus other factors remains uncertain, and multimodal fusion's potential impact cannot be assessed without direct comparison."
}

